  "voting_summary": "Alabama votes almost entirely on election day (94% of the 2024 vote) as it offers no early in-person voting and requires an excuse to vote by mail. Polls close at 8 p.m. Eastern and counting is fast, with near-complete results by late election night. Election day precincts are counted first, then absentee ballots are folded in late in the evening. The small absentee pool is notably less Republican (R+12) than the election day vote (R+32), so late-reporting absentees nudge margins slightly leftward.",
